{
  "abstract": "In `general_pretraining_32/v2` [5], $8\\text{L}\\to 12\\text{L}$ depth growth (`PyrTarget-Medial4`, $71.30\\text{M}$ parameters) beat 953-step static $8\\text{L}$ at nominal FLOPs ($-4.395\\pm 0.368\\text{ mBPB}$ on `Slice B`) at $B=64$, yet trailed 1,068-step uncheckpointed static $8\\text{L}$ by $+2.857\\pm 0.334\\text{ mBPB}$ ($p=0.00336$) when static $8\\text{L}$ received the $+12.04\\%$ analytical executed FLOPs of 6-block checkpointing (`ckpt [2..8)`). Across 65 runs (seeds 42, 137, 271, 314), we study how Squared-ReLU activation deduplication alters this compute-matched comparison. First, under compiled `bfloat16` autocast, compositional `F.relu(z).square()` and custom autograd without explicit output casting retain 5 storages ($1{,}156.0\\text{ MiB}$ per $4d$ MLP at $B=64, T=2{,}048$), whereas `_SqrtBackReLU2Fn` with explicit `.to(z.dtype)` deduplicates the saved post-square tensor with `c_proj`'s input (4 storages, $644.0\\text{ MiB}$; saving $-4{,}096.0\\text{ MiB}$ across $12\\text{L}$ `ckpt [4..8)`), reducing $12\\text{L}$ checkpointing to 2 blocks (`ckpt [6..8)`, $+4.26\\%$ recomputation). While scalar reconstruction $u=R(\\sqrt{\\text{fp32}(R(u^2))})$ is bit-exact across all $16{,}256$ normal-square positive `bfloat16` values ($100\\%$ of $1.777\\times 10^{10}$ positive ClimbMix trajectory activations) and yields $100\\%$ bitwise-equal gradients in eager mode, TorchInductor's fused backward kernel elides the intermediate `.to(bfloat16)` rounding on $\\sqrt{\\text{fp32}(a)}$, shifting $6.25\\%$ of activation gradients by 1 ULP and producing $0.00282$ (`x.grad`) and $0.00415$ (`c_fc.grad`) relative-$L_2$ gradient differences ($0.00245$–$0.00373$ across trained $12\\text{L}$ checkpoints), while matching fixed-step endpoint quality ($+0.056\\pm 0.087\\text{ mBPB}$ at $m=728$, $p=0.564$). Second, reinvesting the saved recomputation budget into 49 extra $12\\text{L}$ steps ($m=777$ vs. $728$) at wall-clock parity ($1{,}248.9\\pm 19.4\\text{ s}$ vs. $1{,}241.0\\pm 18.0\\text{ s}$) improves `PyrTarget-Medial4` by $-5.218\\pm 0.095\\text{ mBPB}$ ($p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.000080$), beating `Static-8L-Unif4d-m1068` by $-2.362\\pm 0.355\\text{ mBPB}$ ($p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.00724$) and width-matched `Static-8L-Pyr8-m1068` by $-1.885\\pm 0.220\\text{ mBPB}$ on `Slice B` ($p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.00724$) and $-1.781\\pm 0.254\\text{ mBPB}$ on untouched `Slice C` ($p=0.00593$, $4/4$ seeds; `long_repeat`: $-22.81\\pm 2.37\\text{ mBPB}$). Post-hoc block-deletion diagnostics and bounded negative screens (`MOFL-12L`, `--vshift-half`) are also reported.",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Addressed all three points from the full review of BFJ2ZzB_erG8DLdl: (1) Removed the claim that compiled _SqrtBackReLU2Fn leaves training dynamics unaltered; prominently reported the isolated-MLP compiled gradient discrepancies (53.72% x.grad and 46.10% c_fc.grad exact match; rel-L2 0.00282 and 0.00415) in Section 2.2 and Table 1B_grad; proved bit-for-bit that TorchInductor fuses the backward pointwise kernel and elides the intermediate .to(bfloat16) rounding on sqrt(fp32(a)) (causing 6.25% 1-ULP shifts on dz while eager _SqrtBackReLU2Fn is 100% bitwise identical to compiled standard ReLU^2); explained why step-0 GPT.init_weights() zeros c_proj and added a 10-step ClimbMix training trajectory audit (35.43B MLP activations) and trained-checkpoint nonzero-c_proj gradient audit (c_fc mean rel-L2 0.00245 at ckpt [4..8) and 0.00373 at ckpt [6..8)); and corrected Table 1 Regime IV to show that 8,064 of 8,192 overflow-square inputs (e in [64, 126], e.g., u=2^64 -> 2u=2^65) have finite standard autograd gradients at unit upstream gradient whereas custom reconstruction from R(u^2)=+inf returns +inf across all 8,192 inputs. (2) Corrected the quarter-budget (s240, accum=2, 262,144 tok/update) schedule description and verification script (compute_exec_flops) to distinguish actual optimizer updates (368 for growth with g=118 [32.1% of updates, 30.93M/96.47M tokens], 480 for Static-8L, 332 for Static-12L) from 524,288-token reference-batch-equivalent steps (184, 240, 166); and reconciled the Stage-1 checkpoint reuse provenance in Section 3.1 and Appendix A (seeds 42, 137, 271 shared bit-identical g=225 checkpoints between m=728 and m=777, whereas seed=314 m=777 in Phase 8 was launched from step 0 with slightly different weight-decay slope 1-t/777 vs 1-t/728, and verified on Slice C rerun within -0.075 mBPB). (3) Centered the title, abstract, and main text on the storage mechanism, its scalar vs. compiled numerical behavior, and the principal True4x64/Slice C confirmation; moved detailed s240 and secondary DEL-ADD/VShift tables to Appendix B; and replaced causal wording in Section 4 with strictly descriptive, associational framing.",
